<p><code>Html\Parser</code> reads HTML and CSS and writes directly into a <code>Document</code> — headings, paragraphs,
lists, links, images and tables become pages, text streams, images and paths, with no headless
browser or external rendering engine anywhere in the path.</p>
<h2 id="converting-a-string-of-html">Converting a String of HTML<a class="anchor" href="#converting-a-string-of-html" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Pdf::importFromHtml()</code> is the fastest way in: hand it a string, get a ready-to-write <code>Document</code>
back.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$html</span> = <span class="text-str">&lt;&lt;&lt;HTML
</span><span class="text-str">&lt;h1&gt;Quarterly Report&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue is &lt;strong&gt;up 12%&lt;/strong&gt; from last quarter, driven largely by
&lt;a href=&quot;https://example.com/report&quot;&gt;the new product line&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;North region: on target&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;South region: ahead of plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</span><span class="text-str">HTML</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">importFromHtml</span>(<span class="text-var">$html</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Reading that PDF back with <code>Pdf::extractTextFromFile()</code> returns every word: &quot;Quarterly Report
Revenue is up 12% from last quarter, driven largely by the new product line. North region: on
target South region: ahead of plan&quot; — one page, nothing dropped.</p>
<p>The table below is what actually came back when each of these tags was rendered and checked, not
what the tag names suggest:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Markup</th>
<th>Behavior</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>–<code>&lt;h6&gt;</code></td>
<td>A block heading, bold, at 32/28/24/20/16/14pt</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;span&gt;</code></td>
<td>A block of text, styled like any other tag by name, <code>id</code> or <code>class</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;strong&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;b&gt;</code></td>
<td>Switches to the bold variant of the current font</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;em&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;i&gt;</code></td>
<td>Parses without error and carries the surrounding weight — reach for <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> or a color to set emphasis apart</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;a href=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code></td>
<td>Inline text, blue by default from the built-in <code>a</code> selector</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;br&gt;</code></td>
<td>A line break inside the current text</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;li&gt;</code></td>
<td>Each <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> is its own line of text; no bullet or number is drawn</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;img src=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code></td>
<td>Placed at the current position, sized from <code>width</code>/<code>height</code> attributes or CSS</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;table&gt;</code> and its row/cell tags</td>
<td>A full grid layout — see <a href="#tables">Tables</a></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>A block reads its own text plus, for every inline tag nested inside it at any depth, that tag's own
text — <code>&lt;p&gt;Normal &lt;strong&gt;bold &lt;em&gt;and italic&lt;/em&gt; tail&lt;/strong&gt; text&lt;/p&gt;</code> renders every word: &quot;Normal
bold and italic tail text&quot;.</p>
<h2 id="converting-a-file">Converting a File<a class="anchor" href="#converting-a-file" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

