<h2 id="using-the-parser-directly">Using the Parser Directly<a class="anchor" href="#using-the-parser-directly" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Pdf::importFromHtml()</code>, <code>importFromHtmlFile()</code> and <code>importFromHtmlUri()</code> are all a thin wrapper
around <code>Html\Parser</code> — construct it directly for anything more than a one-shot conversion:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;h1&gt;Direct Parser&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Body text.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getDocument</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>parseString()</code>, <code>parseFile()</code> and <code>parseUri()</code> are all static:</p>
<ul>
<li>each builds a <code>Parser</code> around the <code>Document</code> passed in (or a fresh one, since both arguments
default), loads the markup, and hands the parser back — nothing is rendered onto the document yet</li>
<li><code>process()</code> is the step that walks the loaded HTML and adds pages, text and images to the document
— call it once parsing and any <code>parseCss*()</code> calls are done</li>
</ul>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.html&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>parseUri()</code> works the same way against a URL instead of a local path — fetching over HTTP was
confirmed against a local <code>php -S</code> server rather than a public host:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseUri</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/report.html&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>Pdf::importFromHtmlUri()</code> is the one-shot equivalent, handing back the <code>Document</code> rather than the
parser.</p>
<p><code>setDocument()</code> and <code>getDocument()</code> are the plain accessors for the <code>Document</code> a parser targets:</p>
<ul>
<li>useful when a parser needs to be pointed at a document built up elsewhere before <code>process()</code> runs</li>
<li><code>parseString()</code>, <code>parseFile()</code> and <code>parseUri()</code> are static factories that build their own <code>Parser</code>
and <code>Document</code> — reach for the instance method <code>parseHtml()</code> instead, to parse into a <code>Document</code> a
parser was already pointed at with <code>setDocument()</code></li>
</ul>
<p>That instance method:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>();
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>   = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>();
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setDocument</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>);

<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Targets the document passed to setDocument().&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/targeted.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Extracting <code>targeted.pdf</code> back out returns &quot;Targets the document passed to setDocument().&quot; — proof
the paragraph landed in the <code>Document</code> instance <code>setDocument()</code> pointed at, not in some other one.</p>
<h2 id="styling">Styling<a class="anchor" href="#styling" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<h3 id="inline-and-embedded-css">Inline and Embedded CSS<a class="anchor" href="#inline-and-embedded-css" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>parseCss()</code> applies a CSS string directly:</p>
<ul>
<li>it stacks with every other <code>parseCss*()</code> call on the same parser</li>
<li>styling a class with <code>background-color</code> proves the stylesheet reached rendering rather than
merely registering — with no CSS applied at all, the same markup draws zero paths on the page;
with the call below, it draws one, a filled box behind the paragraph's text</li>
</ul>
<p>Confirmed by rendering:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p class=&quot;callout&quot;&gt;Read this first.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseCss</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;.callout { background-color: #ffe0b2; padding-top: 4px; padding-bottom: 4px; }&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-fn">count</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getDocument</span>()-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPaths</span>())); <span class="text-comment">// int(1)</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>getCss()</code> reads the accumulated stylesheet back as a <code>Pop\Css\Css</code> object — a quick way to confirm
a selector registered before chasing why it isn't showing up in the rendered page:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Css\Css</span>;

<span class="text-var">$css</span> = <span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getCss</span>();
<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$css</span> <span class="text-kw">instanceof</span> <span class="text-type">Css</span>);              <span class="text-comment">// true</span>
<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$css</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">hasSelector</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;.callout&#039;</span>));    <span class="text-comment">// true</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Style selectors reach the same selector table from three sources:</p>
<ul>
<li>tag name, <code>#id</code> and <code>.class</code></li>
<li>a <code>style=&quot;...&quot;</code> attribute written directly on an element</li>
<li>a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block written into the markup</li>
</ul>
<p>All apply, and the inline <code>style</code> attribute wins over every other selector matching the same element
— the normal CSS cascade:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(
    <span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p style=&quot;color:#ff0000; font-size:30px&quot;&gt;Styled inline.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>,
    <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>()
);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That paragraph's text stream carries <code>30 Tf</code> and <code>1 0 0 rg</code> — the inline attribute's size and color,
not the 12-point black the parser's built-in <code>p</code> selector would otherwise draw.</p>
<p>A <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block written into the markup is read the same way, without a separate call. The sample
below wraps its <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;body&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> because it must: a fragment with a <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> but no
<code>&lt;html&gt;</code> wrapper around it parses to a page with nothing on it — a bare fragment with no <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> at
all renders fine without one.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$html</span> = <span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;style&gt;p { font-size: 28px; color: #0000ff; }&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&#039;</span>
    . <span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Block styled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&#039;</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(<span class="text-var">$html</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The paragraph draws at <code>28 Tf</code> in <code>0 0 1 rg</code> — the <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block's rule, not the built-in default.</p>
<p>A <code>&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code> tag inside <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> loads automatically when
the markup comes from <code>parseFile()</code>, <code>parseHtmlFile()</code> or <code>importFromHtmlFile()</code> — the <code>href</code>
resolves against the HTML file's directory, the same way an <code>&lt;img src&gt;</code> does:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-comment">// invoice.html:  &lt;head&gt;&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;invoice.css&quot;&gt;&lt;/head&gt;</span>
<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">importFromHtmlFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.html&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A tag selector's <code>font-size</code> applies too, alongside <code>.class</code> and <code>#id</code> selectors — <code>p { font-size: 24px; }</code> passed to <code>parseCss()</code> renders every <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> at 24pt, confirmed by the <code>24 Tf</code> the paragraph's
text stream carries afterward.</p>
<h3 id="css-from-a-file">CSS From a File<a class="anchor" href="#css-from-a-file" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>parseCssFile()</code> reads a <code>.css</code> file from disk on its own, independent of whatever HTML is loaded:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Styled from a file.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseCssFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.css&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<h3 id="css-from-a-uri">CSS From a URI<a class="anchor" href="#css-from-a-uri" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>parseCssUri()</code> is the same call against a URL — confirmed here too against a local server rather
than a live host:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-type">Parser</span>::<span class="text-fn">parseString</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Styled from a URI.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseCssUri</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/report.css&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<h3 id="default-styles">Default Styles<a class="anchor" href="#default-styles" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>Every parser starts with the same fallback, before any CSS is applied: <code>Arial</code>, 10-point,
normal weight, black, with a 14-point line height. <code>getDefaultStyles()</code> returns that array, and
<code>setDefaultStyle()</code> changes one entry in it:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setDefaultStyle</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;font-family&#039;</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;TimesNewRoman&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getDefaultStyle</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;font-family&#039;</span>)); <span class="text-comment">// &quot;TimesNewRoman&quot;</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A parser also ships six heading selectors, plus <code>p</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>strong</code> and <code>em</code>, pre-registered before any
markup is parsed:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>h1</code> through <code>h6</code> and <code>p</code> each carry their own <code>font-size</code> (32/28/24/20/16/14pt and 12pt
respectively) on top of the 10-point fallback above</li>
<li><code>h1</code>–<code>h6</code> and <code>strong</code> carry a bold weight that does switch the rendered font (confirmed above)</li>
<li><code>em</code> carries an italic <code>font-style</code> entry that font resolution doesn't act on — see the <code>&lt;em&gt;</code> row
in the markup table above</li>
<li><code>a</code> carries its blue</li>
<li>all of this is independent of any CSS supplied</li>
</ul>
<p><code>setDefaultStyle()</code> reaches <code>font-size</code>, <code>line-height</code> and <code>color</code> the same way a matching selector's
value would, each converting to a real number or color and applying directly:</p>
<ul>
<li>the one exception is ordinary CSS specificity — <code>p</code> and <code>h1</code>–<code>h6</code> each carry their own
pre-registered <code>font-size</code>, so a default there is overruled the way a tag selector is by a more
specific one</li>
<li>every other tag, including <code>div</code>, <code>span</code> and <code>li</code>, takes the default directly</li>
<li><code>color</code> accepts a hex string or an <code>rgb(...)</code> value the same way <code>parseCss()</code> does; anything
outside those formats raises a <code>Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Exception</code> rather than rendering silently</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="page-setup">Page Setup<a class="anchor" href="#page-setup" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<h3 id="page-size">Page Size<a class="anchor" href="#page-size" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>Pages the parser creates default to a 612-by-792-point US Letter page. Set a different one up front
with an additional <code>$pageSize</code> argument for  <code>parseString()</code>, <code>parseFile()</code>, <code>parseUri()</code>,
<code>Pdf::importFromHtml()</code>, <code>importFromHtmlFile()</code> and <code>importFromHtmlUri()</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(), <span class="text-type">pageSize</span>: <span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">A4</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;A4 page.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>();
<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getWidth</span>(), <span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getHeight</span>()); <span class="text-comment">// int(595), int(842)</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A <code>[width, height]</code> array in points takes the place of the constant for a size that has none —
<code>new Parser(new Document(), pageSize: [400, 600])</code>. <code>getPageSize()</code> reports whichever is in effect,
<code>LETTER</code> until something changes it.</p>
<p><code>setPageSize()</code> sets it after construction instead, and passing a <code>$height</code> alongside <code>$size</code> gives
an explicit width and height in points:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageSize</span>(<span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">height</span>: <span class="text-num">900</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Custom page.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>();
<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getWidth</span>(), <span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getHeight</span>()); <span class="text-comment">// int(400), int(900)</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Every page the parser creates from that point on — including the extra pages it adds when content
overflows — uses whichever size was set last.</p>
<h3 id="margins">Margins<a class="anchor" href="#margins" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>The four default margins, measured directly, are 80 points on top, 60 on the right, 60 on the
bottom and 60 on the left. <code>setPageMargins()</code> sets all four at once, and <code>getPageMargins()</code> returns
them as an associative array:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageMargins</span>(<span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-num">50</span>, <span class="text-num">40</span>, <span class="text-num">30</span>);

<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPageMargins</span>()); <span class="text-comment">// [&#039;top&#039; =&gt; 100, &#039;right&#039; =&gt; 50, &#039;bottom&#039; =&gt; 40, &#039;left&#039; =&gt; 30]</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>setPageTopMargin()</code>, <code>setPageRightMargin()</code>, <code>setPageBottomMargin()</code> and <code>setPageLeftMargin()</code> set
one side without touching the other three, and each has a matching getter. <code>getCurrentY()</code> is where
a changed margin actually shows up — it resolves the first page and returns the y-coordinate content
starts at, so a taller top margin moves that starting point down:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageTopMargin</span>(<span class="text-num">120</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageRightMargin</span>(<span class="text-num">45</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageBottomMargin</span>(<span class="text-num">45</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageLeftMargin</span>(<span class="text-num">45</span>);

<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPageTopMargin</span>());  <span class="text-comment">// int(120)</span>
<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getCurrentY</span>());       <span class="text-comment">// int(672), i.e. 792 - 120</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="controlling-flow">Controlling Flow<a class="anchor" href="#controlling-flow" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>The parser tracks an <code>x, y</code> cursor as it walks the HTML — <code>y</code> counts down from the top margin, and
every block advances it by that block's rendered height. <code>setX()</code> and <code>setY()</code> override that cursor
directly, repositioning where the <em>next</em> parsed node starts:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;First block.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setY</span>(<span class="text-num">400</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setX</span>(<span class="text-num">150</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Second block, repositioned.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The first paragraph starts at the left margin, 712 points up from the page's bottom edge on a
default Letter page. The second, after <code>setY(400)</code> and <code>setX(150)</code>, starts at x 150 and y 312 —
exactly <code>792 - 80 - 400</code> — regardless of where the first paragraph left the cursor.</p>
<p><code>getCurrentY()</code> is what the parser calls internally before placing anything: it resolves the current
page — creating the first one, at whatever size and margins are set, if none exists yet — and returns
the y-coordinate the next node would render at. <code>setYOverride()</code> pins the <em>exact</em> y-coordinate the
next node renders at instead, bypassing the accumulated cursor; a <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> uses it internally to hand
flow back at the exact height the table finished at:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Above the override.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setYOverride</span>(<span class="text-num">250</span>);
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Resumes exactly at the override.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The second paragraph starts at y 250 exactly, one call after <code>setYOverride(250)</code> — the same
mechanism is available directly for placing a node at a precise height after adding something to the
page by hand.</p>
<p><code>newPage()</code> adds a fresh page at the parser's current size and margins, resets the cursor to the top
margin, and returns the y-coordinate that fresh page starts at — the parser calls it automatically
whenever content would run past the bottom margin, and it is available directly for a deliberate
page break:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Html\Parser</span>;

<span class="text-var">$parser</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Parser</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Page one.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">newPage</span>();
<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">parseHtml</span>(<span class="text-str">&#039;&lt;p&gt;Page two.&lt;/p&gt;&#039;</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">process</span>();

<span class="text-fn">var_dump</span>(<span class="text-var">$parser</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getDocument</span>()-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getNumberOfPages</span>()); <span class="text-comment">// 2</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="tables">Tables<a class="anchor" href="#tables" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Table\Grid</code> walks a <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> into an explicit row-and-column grid before anything is drawn:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>&lt;thead&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tbody&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;tfoot&gt;</code> rows are read in document order regardless of which section they
sit in</li>
<li>a row counts as a header row when it comes from <code>&lt;thead&gt;</code>, or when every one of its cells is a <code>&lt;th&gt;</code></li>
<li><code>colspan</code> and <code>rowspan</code> claim the extra grid slots a cell covers, so a cell after a <code>colspan=&quot;2&quot;</code>
lands in the correct next column rather than overlapping it</li>
</ul>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$html</span> = <span class="text-str">&lt;&lt;&lt;HTML
</span><span class="text-str">&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Item&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Quantity&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Price&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Widgets (assorted)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;\$19.99&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td rowspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Bulk Order&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;100&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;\$4.50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;250&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;\$4.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
</span><span class="text-str">HTML</span>;

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">importFromHtml</span>(<span class="text-var">$html</span>, <span class="text-type">document</span>: <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>());
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Extracting the result confirms the grid: &quot;Item Quantity Price Widgets (assorted) $19.99 Bulk Order
100 $4.50 250 $4.00&quot; — the colspan cell prints once, spanning the width of the two columns it
covers, and the rowspan cell prints once rather than repeating on the row below it.</p>
<p><code>Table\Layout</code> works in passes:</p>
<ul>
<li>column width: it first measures every cell's natural width from its text and font, taking the
widest cell in each column, then distributes the table's available width across columns
proportionally to those natural widths</li>
<li>a <code>width</code> attribute or CSS <code>width</code> on a single-column cell overrides that column with an explicit
pixel or percentage value instead — <code>&lt;td width=&quot;70%&quot;&gt;</code> on a two-column table gives that column 70%
of the table's width, leaving the rest for the other column</li>
<li>every row is at least 20 points tall regardless of content; a row's actual height is whichever of
its cells needs the most lines to wrap</li>
</ul>
<p>A table too long for one page breaks across as many pages as it needs, and every header row —
<code>&lt;thead&gt;</code> or an all-<code>&lt;th&gt;</code> row — repeats at the top of each new page the table continues onto; an
80-row table under one header row confirmed the header present on all three pages it spread across.</p>
<p><code>drawBox()</code> paints each cell's <code>background-color</code> and <code>border-width</code> before its text, the same
box-drawing a styled <code>&lt;td&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;th&gt;</code> uses outside a table:</p>
<ul>
<li>style the <code>&lt;th&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;td&gt;</code> cells themselves — a selector matching the enclosing <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code> draws nothing</li>
<li>a plain element selector (<code>th { ... }</code>) or a bare class selector (<code>.hdr { ... }</code>) both reach the
cells and draw the box</li>
<li>a compound selector joining the two (<code>th.hdr { ... }</code>) matches nothing — write them as two separate
rules instead</li>
</ul>
